# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing containing source post text is tracked.
#
# The corpus is public forum and video-comment text about people's own health,
# and it is only partially de-identified (see the de-identification note in
# README.md). Sample pools, SFT files, the teacher cache and any annotation
# sheet all carry the post text verbatim, so none of them belong in a
# repository. What is tracked instead is the code that produces them, the
# label-only gold set, and the run metrics.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The corpus itself, wherever it is mounted
data/corpus/
data/*.csv
data/sft/
data/teacher_cache.json
data/teacher_labels*.csv
data/sample_manifest.json

# Annotation sheets: these hold the post text alongside the labels
data/gold/*
!data/gold/gold_blind.csv
!data/gold/gold_blind_sources.csv

# Tracked on purpose: a synthetic corpus so the pipeline runs with no real data
!data/examples/
!data/examples/*

# Tracked on purpose: the redaction word list is a vocabulary, not text
!data/corpus_lowercase_words.json

# Adapter weights: 126 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit. Reproduce with
# `python train.py`; the metrics and eval JSON next to them are tracked.
runs/**/adapter/
runs/**/checkpoint-*/
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.gguf

# Generated prompt artifacts. system.txt is tracked as the teacher prompt of
# record; the other two quote real posts and real cost figures.
prompts/sample_calls.txt
prompts/exposure_report.txt

# Secrets
.env
*.key

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.bak
